	quests: [
		{
			description: [
				"In &6Create: Forge Frontier&r, the mod &5Apotheosis&r overhauls the vanilla enchanting system. It does this by introducing some new stats to enchanting tables and new bookshelves to alter those stats."
				""
				"These stats are as follows:"
				"&n&aEterna&r&r"
				"&n&4Quanta&r&r"
				"&5&nArcana&r&r"
				""
				"Other modifiers that can be added are:"
				"&eRectification&r"
				"&3Enchanting Clues&r"
				"&6Treasure Enchantments&r"
			]
			id: "6965F4ABCAB88875"
			rewards: [{
				id: "48F1F245E472FD1F"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 150
			}]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 2.3d
			subtitle: "Apotheosis Enchanting"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2D29A403707CC3C6"
				item: "minecraft:book"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Introduction to Enchanting"
			x: 5.0d
			y: -7.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["6965F4ABCAB88875"]
			description: [
				"&n&5Apotheosis&r&r makes significant changes to Enchanting in Minecraft, though some core mechanics remain familiar."
				""
				"Enchanting Tables will only detect blocks that modify their stats if those blocks are placed exactly one block away. These stats directly influence the behavior of enchantments."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&a&nEterna&r&r, also known as  Enchanting Power, determines the level of your enchantments. Different tiers and types of bookshelves will add varying amounts. Every shelf has a maximum cap, beyond which additional shelves of that type will not increase the value."
				""
				"The level of your enchantment is 2x your Eterna value. If you reach the maximum of 50 &n&aEterna&r&r you will be enchanting at level 100."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&n&4Quanta&r&r represents the instability of your enchantments. It can be both beneficial and detrimental, as it may increase or decrease the true level applied. "
				""
				"The amount it increases or decreases depends on the enchanting table's Quanta value. If the table has a Quanta value of 50, the actual enchantment value can be -50 or +50."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&n&5Arcana&r&r is the stat that determines the availability of rare enchants. The higher the value is, the easier it is to get rare enchantments."
				""
				"However, very high levels of &5&nArcana&r&r will also make common enchantments more difficult to get."
			]
			id: "2172A6251E7C57A8"
			rewards: [
				{
					exclude_from_claim_all: true
					id: "299E61F0BA970F83"
					table_id: 8678092705658131358L
					type: "choice"
				}
				{
					id: "6931E7D726999DAB"
					type: "xp_levels"
					xp_levels: 2
				}
				{
					count: 10
					id: "08F6E0B772C8A4BA"
					item: "minecraft:bookshelf"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			subtitle: "Enchanting Properties"
			tasks: [{
				id: "62E466E5012D5CCC"
				item: "minecraft:enchanting_table"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Apotheosis Enchanting"
			x: 5.0d
			y: -4.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2172A6251E7C57A8"]
			description: [
				"&n&eRectification&r&r is a modifier that interacts with &4&nQuanta&r&r."
				""
				"It interacts by stripping away the negative side of the random modifier. &4&nQuanta&r&r can both increase and decrease the applied enchantment level, but the higher the Rectification, the smaller the possible decrease. "
				""
				"At 100% &n&eRectification&r&r, enchantments will never go below their base level. Instead, &4&nQuanta&r&r can only increase their strength, even allowing levels to exceed 100 when paired with 50 &a&nEterna&r&r."
			]
			icon: "apotheosis:rectifier"
			id: "722D72A914A3A75B"
			rewards: [
				{
					count: 8
					id: "436B22DE5D260776"
